[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q8-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T8. Recycling of Carbon Dioxide", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 151.06434631347656, 306.6484069824219, 172.77197265625]}, {"text": "7%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.70750427246094, 304.6280822753906, 207.2747344970703]}, {"text": "8.1", "bbox": [127.6520004272461, 209.6475067138672, 141.71697998046875, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.2", "bbox": [159.2779998779297, 209.6475067138672, 173.3429718017578, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.3", "bbox": [190.90399169921875, 209.6475067138672, 204.96897888183594, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.4", "bbox": [222.52999877929688, 209.6475067138672, 236.59498596191406, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.5", "bbox": [254.156005859375, 209.6475067138672, 268.2209777832031, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.6", "bbox": [285.781982421875, 209.6475067138672, 299.8469543457031, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.7", "bbox": [317.40802001953125, 209.6475067138672, 331.4729919433594, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.8", "bbox": [349.0350036621094, 209.6475067138672, 363.0999755859375, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.9", "bbox": [380.6610107421875, 209.6475067138672, 394.7259826660156, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "8.10", "bbox": [411.8500061035156, 209.6475067138672, 431.61358642578125, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "∑", "bbox": [453.62701416015625, 194.75196838378906, 462.7328186035156, 229.34210205078125]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [131.83599853515625, 225.5885009765625, 137.5323944091797, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "16", "bbox": [160.61399841308594, 225.5885009765625, 172.00900268554688, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [195.08799743652344, 225.5885009765625, 200.78439331054688, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "29", "bbox": [223.86599731445312, 225.5885009765625, 235.26100158691406, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "5", "bbox": [258.3399963378906, 225.5885009765625, 264.036376953125, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "10", "bbox": [287.11798095703125, 225.5885009765625, 298.5129699707031, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [321.59197998046875, 225.5885009765625, 327.2883605957031, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [353.2179870605469, 225.5885009765625, 358.91436767578125, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "12", "bbox": [381.9960021972656, 225.5885009765625, 393.3909912109375, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [418.8819885253906, 225.5885009765625, 424.578369140625, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "84", "bbox": [452.4830017089844, 225.5885009765625, 463.87799072265625, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "Removing CO2 gas from the atmosphere is key to combat climate change. One promising solution is the", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 259.41851806640625, 538.571533203125, 275.4767150878906]}, {"text": "photocatalytic reduction of CO2 to CO using molecular catalyst 1.", "bbox": [56.6930046081543, 271.37451171875, 360.442626953125, 287.4327087402344]}, {"text": "8.1", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 373.83551025390625, 92.84233856201172, 387.4027404785156]}, {"text": "Write the half equation for the reduction of CO2 to CO in an acidic medium.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 373.83551025390625, 468.75927734375, 389.89373779296875]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 373.760498046875, 521.8194580078125, 387.3277282714844]}, {"text": "The conjugate oxidation reaction occurs with sacrificial reductant 2 in aqueous solution with the following", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 404.5174865722656, 538.5880737304688, 418.0857238769531]}, {"text": "mechanism:", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 416.4734802246094, 113.63990783691406, 430.04071044921875]}, {"text": "Species 3, 4, and 5 are short-lived ionic and/or radical intermediates. 7 yields a silver mirror with the", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 523.3934936523438, 538.5806884765625, 536.960693359375]}, {"text": "[Ag(NH3)2]OH test.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 520.4329223632812, 146.66201782226562, 555.0230712890625]}, {"text": "8.2", "bbox": [78.60799407958984, 558.3134765625, 92.84233093261719, 571.8806762695312]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of 3-7.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 558.3134765625, 241.50062561035156, 571.8807373046875]}, {"text": "16.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1519775390625, 558.2384643554688, 526.921142578125, 571.8056640625]}, {"text": "Catalyst 1 can be synthesised with the following reaction.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 588.9954833984375, 323.4672546386719, 602.5626831054688]}, {"text": "8.3", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 715.4835205078125, 92.84233856201172, 729.0507202148438]}, {"text": "Tick the correct geometry for the structure of 1.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 715.4835205078125, 339.3226013183594, 729.0507202148438]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 715.4075317382812, 521.8193969726562, 728.9747314453125]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q8-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "When 1 is loaded on crystalline carbon nitride (C3N4) support material, it can reduce CO2 via the following", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5894165039062, 171.27772521972656]}, {"text": "mechanism.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 113.63987731933594, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "8.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 476.32049560546875, 92.84233856201172, 489.8877258300781]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of 9-15. Use the cartoon structure for ligand 8 shown", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 476.32049560546875, 480.58880615234375, 489.8877258300781]}, {"text": "above. For 9-15, specify the oxidation state, 𝑂𝑆, coordination number, 𝐶𝑁,", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 473.3609619140625, 480.5846252441406, 507.95111083984375]}, {"text": "and number of valence electrons, 𝑉𝐸, of Fe, along with the total charge of cor-", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 487.65997314453125, 480.5687255859375, 522.2501220703125]}, {"text": "responding complex structures, 𝑍. Note: Some information is provided on the", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 499.61492919921875, 480.5813903808594, 534.205078125]}, {"text": "answer sheet.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 526.4865112304688, 179.78729248046875, 540.0537109375]}, {"text": "29.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 476.2454833984375, 526.921142578125, 489.8127136230469]}, {"text": "8.5", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 561.8125, 92.84233856201172, 575.3796997070312]}, {"text": "Calculate the number of catalytic molecules per nm2, 𝑁𝑐𝑎𝑡, of C3N4 loaded with", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 546.89697265625, 480.5807800292969, 583.0755615234375]}, {"text": "1, when the mass fraction of catalyst, 𝜔𝑐𝑎𝑡= 3.8%, if the specific surface area of", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 558.8519897460938, 480.5807800292969, 595.0305786132812]}, {"text": "C3N4", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 587.83154296875, 142.3929443359375, 603.5979614257812]}, {"text": "is 17.8 m2 g−1. M𝑐𝑎𝑡= 557.21 g mol−1.", "bbox": [139.81497192382812, 571.4873046875, 321.3186340332031, 609.0946044921875]}, {"text": "5.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 561.737548828125, 521.8194580078125, 575.3047485351562]}, {"text": "The Turnover Frequency of a catalyst (TOF) is the number of product molecules formed per active catalyst", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 617.719482421875, 538.5624389648438, 631.2866821289062]}, {"text": "molecule per hour. Under LED illumination (𝜆= 390 nm) with power of 50 mW, there was a TOF of 8 h−1", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 615.150146484375, 538.0847778320312, 651.1701049804688]}, {"text": "for 10 mg of C3N4, loaded with 1 with 𝜔𝑐𝑎𝑡= 3.8%", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 628.534912109375, 287.4955749511719, 664.7135009765625]}, {"text": "The formula for calculating the quantum yield is given below:", "bbox": [56.69297790527344, 661.3824462890625, 342.6302490234375, 674.9496459960938]}, {"text": "𝜑= 𝑛𝑢𝑚𝑏𝑒𝑟𝑜𝑓𝑟𝑒𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑒𝑑𝑒𝑙𝑒𝑐𝑡𝑟𝑜𝑛𝑠", "bbox": [218.39599609375, 678.55322265625, 346.0124206542969, 715.6761474609375]}, {"text": "𝑛𝑢𝑚𝑏𝑒𝑟𝑜𝑓𝑖𝑛𝑐𝑖𝑑𝑒𝑛𝑡𝑝ℎ𝑜𝑡𝑜𝑛𝑠⋅100%", "bbox": [240.0030059814453, 681.0859985351562, 376.8769226074219, 719.5555419921875]}, {"text": "8.6", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 734.6175537109375, 92.84233856201172, 748.1847534179688]}, {"text": "Calculate the quantum yield, 𝜑(%), for CO formation.", "bbox": [114.69254302978516, 719.7019653320312, 362.6832580566406, 754.2921142578125]}, {"text": "10.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1519775390625, 734.54150390625, 526.921142578125, 748.1087036132812]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q8-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "The diagram below shows the change in the TOF of CO as 𝜔𝑐𝑎𝑡is varied.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 140.30397033691406, 391.1622009277344, 176.48255920410156]}, {"text": "8.7", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 407.23748779296875, 92.84233856201172, 420.8047180175781]}, {"text": "How does the overall rate of CO formation per gram of C3N4 loaded with 1", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 407.23748779296875, 480.5843811035156, 423.29571533203125]}, {"text": "change with increasing 𝜔𝑐𝑎𝑡, within the range 0.1 ≤𝜔𝑐𝑎𝑡≤2.9? Tick the correct", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 404.2769470214844, 480.583984375, 440.4555358886719]}, {"text": "box.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 431.1474914550781, 134.69654846191406, 444.7147216796875]}, {"text": "a) increases", "bbox": [137.36798095703125, 443.10247802734375, 189.7725372314453, 456.6697082519531]}, {"text": "b) decreases", "bbox": [137.36798095703125, 455.0584716796875, 192.2831268310547, 468.6257019042969]}, {"text": "c) doesn't change", "bbox": [137.36798095703125, 467.0134582519531, 214.2595672607422, 480.5806884765625]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 407.1614685058594, 521.8193969726562, 420.72869873046875]}, {"text": "The reduction of CO2 can be accompanied by the reduction of additional protons. The changes in Gibbs", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 496.7044982910156, 538.5443725585938, 512.7626953125]}, {"text": "energy during these two reactions are shown in the diagram.", "bbox": [56.69300842285156, 508.65948486328125, 342.4309997558594, 522.2266845703125]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q8-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "The system was irradiated using different LEDs. The diagram below shows the mole percentages, 𝜒, of", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 431.3599853515625, 538.5763549804688, 465.95013427734375]}, {"text": "H2 and CO produced during the reduction of CO2 under four different conditions: no irradiation (N) and", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 458.2304992675781, 538.5681762695312, 474.2887268066406]}, {"text": "irradiation with red (R), green (G), and blue (B) light.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 470.1864929199219, 297.5993347167969, 483.75372314453125]}]}, {"page": 5, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q8-5", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "8.8", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 502.88153076171875, 92.84233856201172, 516.44873046875]}, {"text": "Tick which of the four conditions, mentioned above, corresponds to a, b, c and", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 502.88153076171875, 480.5822448730469, 516.44873046875]}, {"text": "d in the diagram.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 514.8364868164062, 194.86708068847656, 528.4036865234375]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 502.80548095703125, 521.8194580078125, 516.3726806640625]}]}, {"page": 6, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q8-6", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Photosensitisers (PS) offer some advantages over C3N4 for the reduction of CO2. Mn(I)-containing com-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5735473632812, 171.27772521972656]}, {"text": "plexes combined with PS can achieve ~23% quantum yield. In this system, reductive quenching of the", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 167.17449951171875, 538.5736083984375, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "singlet (S1) and triplet (T1) excited states of a PS by reductant (Red) forms PS•−, which donates electrons", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 154.31114196777344, 538.58544921875, 220.2635498046875]}, {"text": "to CO2 through the Mn(I)-containing complex.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 191.0854949951172, 272.339599609375, 207.1437225341797]}, {"text": "PS(S1) + Red", "bbox": [56.69296646118164, 191.97213745117188, 113.50304412841797, 257.924560546875]}, {"text": "𝑘𝑆", "bbox": [119.00996398925781, 196.15220642089844, 129.050537109375, 228.62290954589844]}, {"text": "−", "bbox": [116.26996612548828, 201.87496948242188, 123.09434509277344, 236.46511840820312]}, {"text": "−", "bbox": [118.39199829101562, 201.87496948242188, 125.21637725830078, 236.46511840820312]}, {"text": "−", "bbox": [123.00468444824219, 201.87496948242188, 129.82907104492188, 236.46511840820312]}, {"text": "→PS•−+ Red•+", "bbox": [125.11676025390625, 191.97213745117188, 200.14137268066406, 257.924560546875]}, {"text": "𝑘𝑆= 2.7 × 109 M−1 s−1", "bbox": [209.14295959472656, 200.4462127685547, 316.1141357421875, 238.05355834960938]}, {"text": "PS(T1) + Red", "bbox": [56.69293212890625, 223.05712890625, 114.99100494384766, 289.0095520019531]}, {"text": "𝑘𝑇", "bbox": [120.49893188476562, 227.3162078857422, 129.74249267578125, 259.7868957519531]}, {"text": "−", "bbox": [117.7589340209961, 232.9599609375, 124.58331298828125, 267.55010986328125]}, {"text": "−", "bbox": [119.84111785888672, 232.9599609375, 126.66549682617188, 267.55010986328125]}, {"text": "−", "bbox": [124.45380401611328, 232.9599609375, 131.27818298339844, 267.55010986328125]}, {"text": "→PS•−+ Red•+", "bbox": [126.52603149414062, 223.05712890625, 201.5503387451172, 289.0095520019531]}, {"text": "𝑘𝑇= 1.5 × 108 M−1 s−1", "bbox": [210.55194091796875, 231.53021240234375, 317.43310546875, 269.1385498046875]}, {"text": "The following Jablonski diagram describes the processes occurring in the PS:", "bbox": [56.69291687011719, 270.4215087890625, 413.7630920410156, 283.9887390136719]}, {"text": "𝜏0(S1) = 2.9 ns and", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 533.198974609375, 145.6915283203125, 569.3775634765625]}, {"text": "𝜏0(T1) = 84 𝜇s, where 𝜏0 is the emission lifetime in the absence of the quencher.", "bbox": [153.95999145507812, 533.198974609375, 527.3516845703125, 569.3775634765625]}, {"text": "8.9", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 571.0795288085938, 92.84233856201172, 584.646728515625]}, {"text": "Calculate the percentage of quenching, 𝜂𝑞, (in %) of S1 and T1 states, when", "bbox": [114.69254302978516, 556.1640014648438, 480.58050537109375, 592.342529296875]}, {"text": "[Red] = 0.1 M. Note: here the values of 𝑘𝐼𝑆𝐶and 𝑘𝑅𝐼𝑆𝐶are negligible.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 568.1189575195312, 443.519775390625, 604.2975463867188]}, {"text": "12.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1519775390625, 571.0034790039062, 526.921142578125, 584.5706787109375]}, {"text": "8.10", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 617.9635009765625, 98.54094696044922, 631.5307006835938]}, {"text": "How do the emission lifetimes of S1 and T1 states change when [Red] increases?", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 617.9635009765625, 480.5787353515625, 634.021728515625]}, {"text": "Tick the correct box.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 629.9185180664062, 210.88375854492188, 643.4857177734375]}, {"text": "a) increases", "bbox": [137.3679962158203, 641.87353515625, 189.77256774902344, 655.4407348632812]}, {"text": "b) decreases", "bbox": [137.3679962158203, 653.8285522460938, 192.2831268310547, 667.395751953125]}, {"text": "c) doesn't change", "bbox": [137.3679962158203, 665.7835693359375, 214.25958251953125, 679.3507690429688]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 617.8875732421875, 521.8194580078125, 631.4547729492188]}]}]